## 2. Agreement, and one correction

The incoming reading of the cut is right on the following points, and all of them are
theorems here:

* the shape inequality `∫q ≤ Λ²∫|q″|` kills the optimized quadratic-decay criterion, since
  it would force `(2J+1)·A·log(|t|+J+4) < π²/18`;
* what survives is the clustering proportion `(4/π²)·highGapMass < lowGapMass`;
* the density bound is `J < 1 + D + π²A(2D+2)/(4c)`.

The correction concerns the consequence for the adaptive regime.  With `D = π/(3Λ)` the
density bound is an *inverse-width* bound with leading coefficient `π/3 + π³A/(6c)`
(`density_cutoff_bound_eq`), and the quarter-period requirement is the inverse-width lower
bound with coefficient `π/2`.  The comparison of the two is now proved:

* `leading_window_nonempty_iff` : `π/2 < π/3 + π³A/(6c) ↔ c < π²A` (for `c > 0`);
* `quarter_period_and_density_window` : the two requirements together force
  `π/2 < π/3 + π³A/(6c) + Λ·(1 + π²A/(2c))`;
* `quarter_period_and_density_force_c_lt` : equivalently `c < π²A + Λ·(6c/π + 3πA)`;
* `no_window_of_density_constants` : the contrapositive, when the density constants are on
  the other side;
* `exists_cutoff_in_window` : if `c < π²A`, an integer cutoff meeting *both* constraints
  exists for every width below an explicit threshold;
* `matched_densities_lt`, `exists_cutoff_in_window_of_matched_densities_width_le_four` :
  for matched constants `0 < c ≤ A` the condition `c < π²A` is automatic (π² > 1) and the
  threshold exceeds 4, so every width `0 < Λ ≤ 4` admits such a cutoff.

So the density cut converts the adaptive route into the constant-window question
`π/2 < J·Λ < π/3 + π³A/(6c) + O(Λ)`; it does not by itself make that route impossible.
The inequality `c < π²A` is proved here as the exact leading-order solvability condition,
and it is derived from the two bounds — it is not attributed to the density theorem alone.

## 3. The counting hypotheses, discharged for ζ (§38)

`Zeta23.RvM.zetaZeroConfig_local_count` supplies, unconditionally, a constant `A_ζ ≥ 1`
with `N(τ, τ+1] ≤ A_ζ·log(|τ|+3)`.  Instantiating with it:

* `zeta_criterion_never` — at ζ's own counting constant the §34 positivity criterion is
  unsatisfiable for every taper, radius, width, height and cutoff.  The shape no-go is
  therefore **not** conditional on a counting hypothesis; it is a statement about the zeta
  zeros;
* `zeta_short_window_count_le` — `N(t−D−1, t+D] ≤ (A_ζ·log(|t|+D+4))·(2D+2)`, proved by
  covering the window with unit windows;
* `gap_split_pos_requires_bounded_cutoff_zeta`, `quarter_period_and_density_force_c_lt_zeta`
  — the §36 and §37 statements with the explicit upper density constant
  `A = A_ζ·log(|t|+D+4)`; only the *lower* density bound of the long window remains a
  hypothesis.

Because `A_ζ ≥ 1` and the logarithm is evaluated at a point `≥ 4`, the resulting bound on
the lower density constant exceeds `π²`, i.e. for ζ the window comparison bites only on an
implausibly large lower density constant.

